<font color="#993322">

<table align='CENTER' cellpadding='2' border='1' cellspacing='2' background='http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif'><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=4&y=2003">This Month</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=3&y=2003">March-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=2&y=2003">February-2003</A></TD></TR><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=1&y=2003">January-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=12&y=2002">December-2002</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=11&y=2002">November-2002</A></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><CENTER><font size=+2>April, 2003</font><BR></center><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Today's Winner is..</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Sunday - April 13th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>~~I need the 4.7 stuff.~~<BR>
Pardon me?<BR>
~~This stuff says 9.4 and I need the 4.7 double sided~~<BR>
Sir, all of our DVD media can contain a maximum of 4.7gigabites of info per recordable surface. The double sided one you're holding can hold a total of 9.4gig.<BR>
~~I know, but I need the 4.7 one; double sided.~~<BR>
Yes Sir, that is what you are holding.  The media in your hand can hold 4.7gig on one side (/point, then flip media over), and 4.7gig on this other side (/point).  The total amount it can hold is 9.4gig.  That's 4.7gig plus 4.7gig.  Both sides, of the double sided media, when counted together hold 9.4gig. (/smile)<BR>
~~So you don't have the 4.7 one?~~<BR>
Maybe I'm not understanding you correctly, Sir.  If you are asking if we have double sided dvd media that holds 2.35gig per side for a total of 4.7gig, I'm afraid we can't help you.  To the best of my knowledge, it does not exist.  The only thing I can think of that might be anything like that would be double sided DVD-RAM media.  Some of those come in 2.6gig per side formats for a total of 5.2gig.  DVD-RAM media, however, usually comes in cartriges, is only usebale with specific devices, and isn't sold here.  Chances are, you're holding what you need; double sided 4.7gig media totaling in 9.4gig of storage.<BR>
<BR>
~~Ok. Since you don't have the 4.7 one I'll go somewhere else.(/storms off)~~
</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Today's Winner is...</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Friday - April 11th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>~~Hello.  I've moved my computer from one end of the room to the other.  Everything's hooked up but the cable modem.  It's still across the room next to the outlet. The old cord won't reach.  How long of a cord do I need?~~

</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Uhhh... ok</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Thursday - April 10th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>So there I am talking to this customer....  He says, "I accidently unplugged my computer while it was on.  I plugged it back in and checked all the cables, but it won't work now. What's wrong with it?"<BR>
<BR>
/em whips out his crystal ball....<BR>
I can understand not knowing stuff about computers.  It doesn't mean that you're stupid, it means you lack the knowledge. BIG difference.  This guy, though, was stupid.  How in the heck did he think that I was gonna be able to diagnose the problem?  I mean, if your VCR croaks do you walk over to the repair shop (without the vcr) and ask the guy ~hey, my vcr's broke. What's wrong with it?~<BR>
<BR>
I use to think that there was such a thing as "common sense".  Now I know it's just a misnomer.  How about those people who say "I want to get a really badarse computer with all the bells and whistles, but I don't wanna spend much money".   Duhhh.....  Yeah.  I wanna go on a cruise, be limo'd home to my penthouse appartment, have the buttler take my things to their respctive places, and finish the evening by kicking back and watching some 10foot by 21foot plasma tv; all for 5bucks.  You know what.. it's not gonna happen.  You got 100bucks, you get 100bucks worth of stuff.  Simple, really.  You have 2000 bucks, you can get 2000bucks worth of stuff.  It's not that hard to understand. /smack some ppl.<BR>
<a href="http://pub148.ezboard.com/flegerdemainfrm7.showMessage?topicID=107.topic" target="_rant">Members should feel free to add their comments to the rant area of our boards</a></font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Isn't that special</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Thursday - April 10th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>I'd just like to say that I'm really glad you have all done so well recently.  Legerdemain has been hard hit by harsh work hours, people leaving for bigger and badder guilds, departures from EQ entirely and the like.  Even so, we've gotten 3 more epic members within the past 10days.  We've had a lot of little fun events that everyone seems to have enjoyed greatly.<BR>
<BR>
It's times like this that make it all worth while.  I hope the momentum keeps up and everyone continues to have a great time in-game.  That's what it's all about, after all.  Tiny golden fists, ToV, Kael, CT gnome/RoFear , AC RoFire, or any number of other events are completely doable for Legerdemain.  Two groups would even be enough to hack around in a lot of places.  The bigger ones could be taken when we have closer to 4 or 5 groups on-line hehe.<BR>
<BR>
Speaking of larger groups of Leger's on-line, I'd like to talk about recruitment.  For those who still have trouble finding someone in-guild to group with, try searching for an unguilded 50th+ person out there to duo with hehe.  Evaluate the person as you group.  Group with them again and again over the next few weeks if you can.  If they seem like someone who would fit-in to Legerdemain, talk it up :> Let them know what kind of environment we have and see if it sounds interresting to them.  If not, oh well.  At least you've had some fun and made a new friend eh?<BR>
<BR>
Now, many have said ~If they're 50+ and unguilded, something is wrong.~  This can be true in some cases.  It's also true that several guild's have broken up recently and they could easily be people that are looking for a new home.  I've heard people complain that they're bored, nothing to do, can't get a group, or feeling alone; not in /guildsay, but here and there.  Mostly it happens because there are so few of us.  Hard to find times that line-up for everyone.  I'm sure you've heard it all before but it doesn't change the fact that it may be hard for some people to get groups.<BR>
<BR>
Make one!  That's right :> Walk down to the nearest shopkeeper and buy a pair /nod.  Start sending tells to LFG people.  Gather forces and have some fun.  We're all too spoiled from grouping in-guild hehe.  Meet the people, man.<BR>
<BR>
Now, I'm not hosting some huge campaigne to recruit hundreds of members.  I've never wanted to be a zerg guild.  One applicant every week or two would be fine.  It would help offset any loses, introduce some fresh perspectives, and slowly bolster our numbers as we tackle tougher challenges. /rar!</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Vranican ist epic too!!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Wednesday - April 9th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Ketrel had tried very hard to get his bard epic'd before Tyre but alas! heheh.  One failure on Monday but a big Trak SPANK on Wednesday :> Congrats Ketrel/Vranican.  My only regret is that I wasn't able to be there for the win hehe. /bird work</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Tyre is Epic!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Monday - April 7th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Yup, Tyre is epic now hehe.  After many long hours of camping tedeous mobs and groveling around in KC and CD, Tyre is now EPIC!  After the undead bard attempt in sebilis, a couple groups wandered over to LoIO for a quick SPANK on Xenevorash. The final battle didn't take much time and I'm glad Tyre is now all bubbly :>  </font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR>



</font>
</TD>
